    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d119">

                <pb facs="0173" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.41D112A/5: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ireland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dublin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-18T15:00:00+01:00">April 18, 1944—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>86. Department’s telegram 72, April 15, 5 p.m. Legation opinion expressed in
                    airgram A–44 August 16, 1943<anchor n="36" xml:id="d119-f1"/> regarding
                    extension of Proclaimed List to this country has not changed. Desirability of
                    inclusion in next month’s supplement is not, in our view, affected by the
                    situation resulting from the recent exchange of notes and no objection is seen
                    here to such inclusion.</p>
                <p>The Proclaimed List may include all names now on the Statutory List.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
